"""Hand-written claim specifications: which passage (work + anchor) supports which date for which event or era boundary.

Each spec names an anchor, not a passage: `build_history_candidates.py` finds the anchor in the downloaded text, cuts the
verbatim passage and locator, and refuses the claim unless `stated` (the date as the source words it) occurs in the
passage or, for annals, in the year heading the passage sits under. Years are Hijri. See README.md §Method.

Fields: target ('event', seed title) | ('epoch', id, 'start'|'end') | ('new', key); work; anchor (Arabic, folded for
search; regex allowed); nth (which hit); heading (folded substring the hit's section heading must contain); before/after
(sentence window); entry (cut the whole rijal entry); stated; year, year_max; month_day; qualifier; attributed_to
(the authority the work reports, when it names one); note; flags.
"""


def claim(target, work, anchor, stated, year, **fields):
    spec = {'target': target, 'work': work, 'anchor': anchor, 'stated': stated, 'year': year}
    spec.update(fields)
    return spec


E = lambda title: ('event', title)  # noqa: E731
S = lambda epoch: ('epoch', epoch, 'start')  # noqa: E731
F = lambda epoch: ('epoch', epoch, 'end')  # noqa: E731
N = lambda key: ('new', key)  # noqa: E731

